{"id":"dfb600edb68ffc97f44fddb783033407","name":"test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread[True]","start":1794843593687,"stop":1794843593790,"duration":103,"status":"passed","fullName":"tests.unit_tests.test_bg_job_register#test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread","retryHash":"3b8b4af1a7ac9dec8847283961634708.8ee89f01f3f42a039f3321f8d56d17b0","testCaseHash":"3b8b4af1a7ac9dec8847283961634708","parametersHash":"8ee89f01f3f42a039f3321f8d56d17b0","environmentHash":null,"flaky":false,"muted":false,"known":false,"isRetry":false,"labels":[{"name":"tag","value":"asyncio"},{"name":"parentSuite","value":"tests.unit_tests"},{"name":"suite","value":"test_bg_job_register"},{"name":"host","value":"ip-10-0-134-73"},{"name":"thread","value":"3482-MainThread"},{"name":"framework","value":"pytest"},{"name":"language","value":"cpython3"},{"name":"package","value":"tests.unit_tests.test_bg_job_register"}],"groupedLabels":{"tag":["asyncio"],"parentSuite":["tests.unit_tests"],"suite":["test_bg_job_register"],"host":["ip-10-0-134-73"],"thread":["3482-MainThread"],"framework":["pytest"],"language":["cpython3"],"package":["tests.unit_tests.test_bg_job_register"]},"parameters":[{"name":"from_threadpool","value":"True","hidden":false,"excluded":false,"masked":false}],"links":[],"steps":[{"link":{"id":"9a165440bdeff7f770af72ecacbf0509","originalFileName":"987b3aae-8222-46ce-8acf-e0696dddb09e-attachment.txt","ext":".txt","name":"log","contentType":"text/plain","used":true,"missed":false,"contentLength":201},"type":"attachment"}],"error":{},"testCase":{"id":"3b8b4af1a7ac9dec8847283961634708","externalId":"b26b2803a1572059e3c99b23587b1127","name":"test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread[True]","fullName":"tests.unit_tests.test_bg_job_register#test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread"},"descriptionHtml":"<p>A job finishing in its worker thread must wake the WS waiter in the main loop.</p>\n<pre><code>``run_command`` runs the job in a separate thread with its own event loop, but\nthe ``new_log_evt`` waiters live in the daemon loop. ``asyncio.Event.set()`` is\nnot thread-safe, so without hopping back onto the daemon loop the terminal DONE\nnotification is lost and ``ws_poll_info`` hangs forever (the desktop app's\n&quot;finalizing&quot; step never completes and the connection eventually drops).\n``from_threadpool`` mimics sync routes (``/update/start``), which call\n``run_command`` from FastAPI's threadpool, with no running loop.\n</code></pre>\n","environment":"default","setup":[{"id":"4ae6d196b88cd641276ffddcef3a94de","type":"before","name":"event_loop_policy","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"8a4cd0deb99e3768a335afe4a1c01ed9","type":"before","name":"tmp_path_factory","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"fa670a6b575ff9e96aacce86287ec292","type":"before","name":"monkeypatch","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"78385dba1b71f80a9888928d8542637f","type":"before","name":"_no_telemetry","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"f774bd9ba0099fd0472658db5d229095","type":"before","name":"_isolated_hf_credentials","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":1},{"id":"ddd1765c12bc8951d742ba1f9c5e611a","type":"before","name":"_function_scoped_runner","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":1}],"teardown":[{"id":"5e1765a49a754c2660300a26c2847217","type":"after","name":"_function_scoped_runner::0","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":1},{"id":"e2d3c3eec094edd949470c7573a76724","type":"after","name":"monkeypatch::0","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0}],"history":[{"id":"1671326b9da9e4e8cfa6015e4a175f18","name":"test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread[True]","fullName":"tests.unit_tests.test_bg_job_register#test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread","environment":"default","status":"passed","retries":[],"start":1794843332083,"stop":1794843332187,"duration":104,"labels":[{"name":"tag","value":"